# Go build output for the WebRTC sidecar
webrtc/sage-voice-webrtc

# The WhatsApp bridge's dependency tree. Restored by
# scripts/provision-whatsapp-bridge.sh, pinned by whatsapp/package-lock.json,
# which IS committed — the lock file is the reproducible part.
whatsapp/node_modules/

# WhatsApp session state. Its real home is
# ~/Library/Application Support/SAGE Voice Bridge/WhatsApp/, outside the
# repository, and these patterns exist for the day somebody points --session
# at a checkout while debugging. Committing it would publish a live WhatsApp
# login: anyone holding creds.json is signed in as the owner, and a git
# history does not forget.
whatsapp/session/
**/creds.json
**/app-state-sync-*.json
**/pre-key-*.json
**/session-*.json
**/sender-key-*.json

# Built by scripts/build-opus.sh, not committed: an unreviewable binary in a
# repository is provenance nobody can check.
third_party/
.opus-build/

# The Linux per-test harness's scratch root (scripts/linux-test.sh). Kept out of
# .build/ deliberately: the same checkout is mounted into a Linux container while
# a Mac toolchain owns .build/, and two triples sharing one scratch root is a
# failure that surfaces as nonsense module errors hours later.
.build-linux/
